KZ2 patch 2120: count first-use hitches and keep every session's pipeline template.

First-use shader stutter. Hand play stalls 0.2-0.9 s in the first minute of each area: every new
pipeline is built while the walker waits (patch 2058 awaits each asynchronous build, max-in-flight 1, ~70 ms per
pipeline; 170 builds in the first minute of Corinth River in the maintainer's 2026-10-22 log). Patch 2071's template prewarm
removes them on a first play, but KZ2 shipped no template and had no way to grow one from real sessions.

1. rsx_pace.h (patch 2072): the [pace] line ends with slow100=<intervals of 100 ms or more in the window>, and every
   such interval prints `[hitch] t=<ms since first present> dt=<ms>`, so a run can be cut at the level start.
2. rsx_live_draw.c (patch 2071's ld_pt_start): with LD_PSO_TEMPLATE_OUT unset, the export is on and writes
   <shader cache dir>\pso-template-own.bin, read back first so it grows across sessions (as pso_keys.bin does).
   LD_PSO_TEMPLATE_OUT=<file> keeps KZ3's behaviour (this session only); LD_PSO_TEMPLATE_OUT=0 turns it off.
   tools/runtime/pso_template.py merges the files of several sessions into the shipped pso-template.bin.
3. rsx_pso_template.h + rsx_live_draw.c: the record carries two inputs of the pipeline key it lacked, the WPOS flip
   height (KZ2 patch 2090) and the VP branch bits (upstream #485); without them every pipeline that used either failed
   the prewarm's key recompute (kz2-r47-b1: 247 "key mismatch" against 168 built from a 607-pipeline template). The
   record is 564 bytes now; a template of the old size is refused by its header.

